# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend dev/runtime config.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) to override per-machine defaults.
# Vite reads `.env*` at startup; restart the dev server after editing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the SPA sends every `/api/*` call.
#
# DEFAULT (left empty): the SPA uses relative URLs. In `npm run dev`, that means
# Vite proxies `/api` → http://localhost:5099 (see vite.config.ts). Same-origin,
# no CORS preflight, OAuth callback works at /api/credentials/oauth/callback
# under the SPA's own port.
#
# An OAuth connect comes back to the origin the page was opened on when the
# API lists it: App:PublicBaseUrl, Cors:AllowedOrigins, OAuth:CallbackUrl's own
# origin, and in Development both http://localhost:5180 and the
# http://127.0.0.1:5180 Vite prints. On an origin the API does not list (a LAN
# IP, a tunnel host), the connect still starts, but its popup comes back to the
# host OAuth:CallbackUrl names and stays open there with the outcome; list the
# origin in Cors:AllowedOrigins, or connect from that host.
#
# DIRECT MODE (this var set to a full origin): every API call goes to that
# origin directly, skipping the Vite proxy. Useful when you want to:
#   - hit a backend running on a different host (LAN dev, remote tunnel)
#   - hit a local API that isn't on 5099 (custom port, container)
#   - debug CORS in dev with the same path the production deploy will use
#
# Requirements when you set this:
#   1. The backend's `Cors:AllowedOrigins` (appsettings) must list this SPA's
#      origin — http://localhost:5180 and http://127.0.0.1:5180 are added
#      automatically in Development, anything else needs an explicit entry.
#      An OAuth connect may return to any origin on that list, so this entry
#      is also what lets the OAuth popup come back to this SPA.
#   2. The backend's `OAuth:CallbackUrl` may point at the API itself (e.g.
#      http://localhost:5099/api/credentials/oauth/callback). When the browser
#      cannot keep the connect's binding cookie — the API on another site, or
#      a connect started on another host than the callback URL names — the
#      callback hands the connect to this SPA's /oauth-callback page, which
#      finishes it as the signed-in user who started it.
#   3. For the HttpOnly session cookie, the API must be on the SAME SITE as
#      the SPA (same host name; ports may differ): http://localhost:5180 →
#      http://localhost:5099 works, http://127.0.0.1:5180 → localhost does
#      not. On another site the browser withholds the SameSite=Strict cookie
#      and the SPA keeps its bearer token in localStorage instead — it still
#      works, without the protection the cookie adds.
#
VITE_API_URL=
